# Build context for h-bootstrap and the six services. Their context is this
# whole directory, because each image needs the shared package in
# z-lib/nus-common and the Avro schemas in c-infra-kafka/schemas as well as
# its own code.
#
# The reason this file exists is secrets. Without it every .env in this tree
# is handed to the Docker daemon on each build, and a build context is not a
# private thing — it is uploaded whole, and anything in it can end up in an
# image by a careless COPY. Only the .example templates ever belong here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*/.env
*/.env.*
!*/.env.example

# Host-side Python artefacts. Nothing in an image may come from these: the
# dependencies are installed in the build stage from uv.lock, and a stray
# __pycache__ built by another interpreter would be silently shadowing it.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# The OSM extract is downloaded onto a volume at run time and is hundreds of
# megabytes. It must never reach a build context.
**/*.osm
**/*.osm.pbf

# The superseded first-draft generator, kept only as a reference.
sketch/

# Version control and editor state.
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
